{
  "id": "3kgc3yh",
  "title": "CHAPTER 5 : RATIO AND PROPORTION .",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "tl1ye9u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Meaning of Ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter",
          "value": "Chapter 5",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Primary Topic",
          "value": "Ratio & Proportion",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Solved Example Sum",
          "value": "₹2000",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Percentage Increment",
          "value": "25%",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "kb6hqua"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3g40s6t",
      "content": "A ratio is a comparison between two quantities using division. It tells us how many times one quantity contains another."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8tulln2",
      "content": "Ratio is written as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "euja7hz",
      "content": "a : b or  a/b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h2d59r6",
      "content": "Important Rules:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2j25azt",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Both quantities must be in the same units.</li><li>Ratio has no unit.</li><li>Order matters.</li></ul>",
        "Both quantities must be in the same units.",
        "Ratio has no unit.",
        "Order matters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ek3z4a4",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4atle15",
      "content": "Find the ratio of 4 kg to 500 grams."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xerv1m5",
      "content": "Step 1: Convert into same units. 4 kg = 4000 grams"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "znknnbc",
      "content": "Step 2: Form ratio. 4000 : 500"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "morpfm9",
      "content": "Step 3: Simplify."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sym8qju",
      "content": "Divide by 500 → 8 : 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k5kwdo6",
      "content": "Final Answer: 8 : 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "zbkcmlz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Simplifying Ratios"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "63pe828",
      "content": "Ratios must always be reduced to their lowest form using the Highest Common Factor (HCF)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n1jyvgm",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vxub8o1",
      "content": "Simplify 30 : 45."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sttzc9g",
      "content": "Step 1: HCF of 30 and 45 is 15."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2jsotuh",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3kt9fzu",
      "content": "30 ÷ 15 = 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7b9o2ra",
      "content": "45 ÷ 15 = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ttgtwv2",
      "content": "Final Answer: 2 : 3"
    },
    {
      "id": "0owjs5d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Equivalent Ratios"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bvg141s",
      "content": "If both terms are multiplied or divided by the same number, the ratio remains unchanged."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b64o89f",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3dqwxu",
      "content": "Check whether 6 : 8 and 15 : 20 are equivalent. "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "14jndfg",
      "content": "Step 1: Simplify both ratios."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f5pggli",
      "content": "6 : 8 → divide by 2 → 3 : 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "enhihkc",
      "content": "15 : 20 → divide by 5 → 3 : 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "072ujsj",
      "content": "Final Answer: Yes, they are equivalent."
    },
    {
      "id": "vmff6hz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Ratios"
    },
    {
      "id": "b2ul5af",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Duplicate Ratio – square of terms (a² : b²)</li><li>Sub-duplicate Ratio – square root of terms</li><li>Triplicate Ratio – cube of terms</li><li>Compound Ratio – product of multiple ratios</li></ul>",
        "Duplicate Ratio – square of terms (a² : b²)",
        "Sub-duplicate Ratio – square root of terms",
        "Triplicate Ratio – cube of terms",
        "Compound Ratio – product of multiple ratios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vefk2n1",
      "content": "Example (Triplicate):"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pcakr6r",
      "content": "Find the triplicate ratio of 2 : 5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9n42f7d",
      "content": "Step 1: Cube both numbers. 2³ = 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "h3nnmpd",
      "content": "5³ = 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n7g7x52",
      "content": "Final Answer: 8 : 125"
    },
    {
      "id": "c746z66",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio in Fraction Form"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f092md7",
      "content": "A ratio can be expressed as a fraction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b3iq2v8",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sojvwcb",
      "content": "In a class, boys : girls = 3 : 7. Find the fraction of boys."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wmkaktl",
      "content": "Step 1: Total parts = 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s3b3u4b",
      "content": "Step 2: Boys = 3 parts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wiat0n9",
      "content": "Fraction = 3/10."
    },
    {
      "id": "fwy0jxj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Dividing a Quantity in a Given Ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6hneode",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0jwactw",
      "content": "Divide ₹960 between A and B in ratio 5 : 7. Step 1: Add ratio parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kl3qn4h",
      "content": "5 + 7 = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nnzr0zr",
      "content": "Step 2: Value of one part. 960 ÷ 12 = 80"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j0lh8pp",
      "content": "Step 3: Shares."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "my30f3s",
      "content": "A = 5 × 80 = 400"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9avi6cj",
      "content": "B = 7 × 80 = 560"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5t6nj06",
      "content": "Verification:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "13xfuln",
      "content": "400 + 560 = 960 ✔"
    },
    {
      "id": "napgvd2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Division Among Three Quantities"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "smfq3nd",
      "content": "Example: Divide ₹1800 among A, B, and C in ratio 2 : 4 : 6."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3igwk1w",
      "content": "Step 1: Sum = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tsll900",
      "content": "Step 2: One part = 1800 ÷ 12 = 150"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1lws772",
      "content": "Shares:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qem8tmf",
      "content": "A = 300"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pr9x8bh",
      "content": "B = 600"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8gqfh5v",
      "content": "C = 900"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Divide ₹2000 between A and B so that A gets 25% more than B.",
      "id": "hashnjn"
    },
    {
      "id": "bqgba3y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Numbers from Ratio and Sum"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kfi7ial",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l97lzx3",
      "content": "Two numbers are in ratio 4 : 9 and their sum is 65. Step 1: Let numbers be 4x and 9x."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o7h2las",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1vexzgl",
      "content": "13x = 65"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "e1ymbwc",
      "content": "x = 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pqi4nzz",
      "content": "Numbers:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "96vf5vd",
      "content": "20 and 45."
    },
    {
      "id": "80wzh8u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Finding Numbers from Ratio and Difference"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dvkyvhu",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sd0dyd3",
      "content": "Numbers are in ratio 5 : 8 and difference is 21."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ioompvt",
      "content": "Step 1: Difference = 3x"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g6uuml1",
      "content": "3x = 21"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vu6nfeb",
      "content": "x = 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7ka3j15",
      "content": "Numbers: 35 and 56."
    },
    {
      "id": "6gtuxfy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio When Quantities Change"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qiwrqxl",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cj1pnyq",
      "content": "Ratio of boys to girls is 3 : 4. If 6 boys join, ratio becomes 9 : 4. Find original boys."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8u2tik2",
      "content": "Step 1: Boys = 3x"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mmf70p5",
      "content": "Step 2: 3x + 6 = 9x"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "knsun8v",
      "content": "6 = 6x"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7kjhsd0",
      "content": "x = 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vnd1hqy",
      "content": "Original boys = 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "7k55rx2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Proportion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qwq6asp",
      "content": "When two ratios are equal, they form a proportion. a : b = c : d"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t0ubj25",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3z1okwz",
      "content": "Check if 4 : 6 = 10 : 15."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m6orq6q",
      "content": "4/6 = 2/3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "x6cpaw7",
      "content": "10/15 = 2/3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f4ci45o",
      "content": "Yes, they are in proportion."
    },
    {
      "id": "g3bfyho",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Cross Multiplication Rule"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a8chopw",
      "content": "If a/b = c/d → ad = bc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xldbc3m",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3p4jqpb",
      "content": "Find x if 8 : x = 32 : 12. 8/x = 32/12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "403d7gy",
      "content": "Cross multiply: 8 × 12 = 32x"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "v9i0y1b",
      "content": "96 = 32x"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "074ayjg",
      "content": "x = 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "c1fw2y7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Mean Proportional"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "75vff4b",
      "content": "If a : x = x : b, then x = √ab."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rfhirkf",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pzezky2",
      "content": "Find mean proportional between 9 and 25."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mtr6cot",
      "content": "√(9×25) = √225 = 15."
    },
    {
      "id": "ra3t55t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Third Proportional"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n4q7z8j",
      "content": "If a : b = b : x, then x = b² / a."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tkxjl1p",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cn3cnr4",
      "content": "Find third proportional to 6 and 12."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "en0pxrl",
      "content": "12² = 144"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sxaj30s",
      "content": "144 ÷ 6 = 24."
    },
    {
      "id": "9dks863",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Inverse Ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hbl7b3r",
      "content": "If one quantity increases while another decreases, they are inversely proportional."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l37vwn8",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u64mgvl",
      "content": "If 5 workers complete a task in 20 days, how many days will 10 workers take?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aq6n3wx",
      "content": "5 × 20 = 10 × x"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o3eyrjb",
      "content": "100 = 10x"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ni6bj1m",
      "content": "x = 10 days."
    },
    {
      "id": "8y14yog",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Continued Proportion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v6om42e",
      "content": "If a : b = b : c, then b² = ac."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tli1wt5",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wktmbv9",
      "content": "Find c if 2 : 6 = 6 : c."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ursxalo",
      "content": "2c = 36"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dnuh7uy",
      "content": "c = 18."
    },
    {
      "id": "9z56yvv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio and Percentage Relationship"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fgv71n2",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lyyxiyu",
      "content": "If A : B = 8 : 5, find how much percent A is greater than B. Difference = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e0rkjmb",
      "content": "Compare with B: 3/5 × 100 = 60%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3vtqrkw",
      "content": "A is 60% greater."
    },
    {
      "id": "qap8z0o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Age-Based Ratio Problems"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xlhrm1l",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4vkwy0k",
      "content": "Present ages of A and B are in ratio 2 : 3. After 6 years, ratio becomes 3 : 4. Let ages = 2x and 3x."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4r4hiu7",
      "content": "(2x+6)/(3x+6) = 3/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0j90c7l",
      "content": "Cross multiply:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions on Mean Proportional, Third Proportional, and Continued Proportion are frequently asked in tier-1 competitive exams.",
        "Pay special attention to 'Ratio When Quantities Change' and 'Division Among Three Quantities' as they carry high weightage.",
        "Expressing percentage increments (e.g., A gets 25% more than B) directly as ratios (5:4) saves critical calculation time."
      ],
      "id": "vcaxu0b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qw75yt3",
      "content": "8x + 24 = 9x + 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qidl1gw",
      "content": "x = 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wdqa5rw",
      "content": "A = 12 years"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6og3k6d",
      "content": "B = 18 years."
    },
    {
      "id": "wzgmrw7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Important Examiner Tips"
    },
    {
      "id": "lvsa7ac",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Always assume ratios as multiples (ax, bx).</li><li>Simplify answers.</li><li>Compare with correct base.</li><li>Check whether relation is direct or inverse.</li></ul>",
        "Always assume ratios as multiples (ax, bx).",
        "Simplify answers.",
        "Compare with correct base.",
        "Check whether relation is direct or inverse."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "yl74n83",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOLVED EXAMPLES (CLASSROOM STYLE)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ratio involves simplifying, expressing in fraction forms, finding equivalent forms, and understanding various types of ratios.",
        "Proportion concepts include the Cross Multiplication Rule, Mean Proportional, Third Proportional, and Continued Proportion.",
        "Practical ratio applications include dividing quantities among two or three parts, handling sum/difference conditions, and solving age-based problems.",
        "Percentage relationships can be directly translated into ratios to simplify competitive exam problem solving."
      ],
      "id": "euq8l06"
    },
    {
      "id": "kob46b5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Solved Example: Divide ₹2000 between A and B so that A gets 25% more than B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a6jsms1",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the statement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n7gh3zq",
      "content": "If A gets 25% more than B, it means A is 125% of B. Step 2: Assume a convenient value."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "131m211",
      "content": "Let B = 100 units. Then A = 125 units."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jjks2j2",
      "content": "Step 3: Form the ratio. A : B = 125 : 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3snzhjs",
      "content": "Simplify by dividing both numbers by 25: A : B = 5 : 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m4mhuy4",
      "content": "Step 4: Add ratio parts. 5 + 4 = 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4kjin9w",
      "content": "Step 5: Find the value of one part."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x4dhlfn",
      "content": "2000 ÷ 9 = 222.22 (approx.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yqty81p",
      "content": "Step 6: Find individual shares."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mccbmqy",
      "content": "A = 5 × 222.22 ≈ 1111.11"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a3rzdo1",
